WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.190
<i>The National Public Unified 
Intelligence Matrix.</i>

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.470
<i>It oversees all public 
institutions within Japan.</i>

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.820
<i>A depository of all information 
existing in Japan,</i>

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.150
<i>the system is the beating heart of the nation.</i>

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.520
<i>And it was taken over by Logos.</i>

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.400
<i>With Japan in its grasp,</i>

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.060
<i>Logos halted the entire transportation 
and communications infrastructure,</i>

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:26.010
<i>leaving only the bare minimum to 
sustain life in metropolitan areas.</i>

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.450
<i>At that point, the government 
declared a state of emergency.</i>

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:35.150
<i>A 24-hour curfew was instituted for 
all vehicles, save a few exceptions,</i>

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.320
<i>and citizens were prohibited from 
leaving home after 8 PM.</i>

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.910
<i>Systems are designed to acquiesce 
to figures of greater authority.</i>

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.690
<i>However, such authority isn't necessarily 
designated by the system itself.</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:57.700
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.080
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.740
<b>File 11: Japan Style</b>

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.700
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.870
I guess the TV networks are still down.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.310
Any luck there?

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.520
The same.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.480
I can use it offline, but when I try 
to connect to the Internet...

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.410
<i>I can't seem to connect, sorry.</i>

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.800
<i>I can't seem to connect, sorry.</i>

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.890
The police radio's still down, too...

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.350
But there is a silver lining here.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:50.320
Since Unit 8 was about to be shut down,

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.290
the command vehicle was cut off from 
the network, and escaped damage.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:57.280
Our Wears can communicate with 
each other through radio.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.120
Right?

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.890
Radio comms haven't been compromised?

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:01.440
Analog radio's fine.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.160
Digital radio is out, though.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.400
Do we have any other information?

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.120
Anything, council-related or not.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.960
The only odd thing is a rumor about a ghost 
appearing in the dead of night.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:14.290
A ghost?

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:15.420
What's that about?

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:19.410
There have been sightings reported 
in Ogikubo and Kamishakujii.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:24.140
They say it's a dead ringer for Liko-chan, 
so die-hard fans are sneaking out for a peek.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.370
A peek? But no one's supposed 
to be out after 8 PM!

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.550
Wh-What's up with her?

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.160
She's frustrated because 
she can't do stuff online.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.650
Oh, that must be tough, all right.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:41.660
Come to think of it,

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:45.660
a newspaper journalist I know mentioned 
that the governor's been hospitalized.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.400
Maybe he's just running 
away from this hot mess.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.500
It'd be front-page news any other day, but...

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.880
When presses can't print or deliver papers, 
they can't do anything with that information.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:58.340
Boss!

00:03:58.730 --> 00:03:59.790
Asami-chan?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.940
What were you doing here?

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.010
If you'd let me know beforehand— 
Oh, I guess that's not possible.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.990
I wanted to attend Hachijou 
Tomoki's questioning.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.330
Hachijou's?

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.510
I was hoping to get information 
about his co-conspirators...

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.770
But it was a waste of time.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.730
They wouldn't even tell me about 
their lines of questioning.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.340
They probably don't have anything 
concrete to share with you.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:27.230
Hachijou seems to be engaging them 
in intricate debate and wordplay.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.040
Play?

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.130
After reducing society to this?

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:34.210
How's your sister, by the way?

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:35.960
She must be in shock.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:39.120
Well, I can't say she's doing all right.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.440
After all, her senpai in the student 
council was responsible for this.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:43.830
Kazari-kun.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.440
Director?

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.140
Come with me. Hachijou's asking for you.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.350
Huh?

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.990
In just three days, 
the nation has been decimated.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:56.400
If the state of emergency continues,

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.150
it could even result in 
a global financial crisis.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.580
What's so funny?

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.430
Well, you're saying the same 
things as the other detectives.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.830
I'm disappointed.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:10.160
I thought the youngest assistant inspector 
would understand me a bit better.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.750
So you requested me for 
a conversation partner?

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.080
I dislike boredom.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:19.180
Did you sacrifice yourself 
for your collaborators?

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.230
Sacrifice?

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:24.660
You volunteered yourself as bait to buy time 
for your collaborators to seize control

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.760
of the National Public 
Unified Intelligence Matrix,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.650
and delay police action, if only temporarily.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:31.390
Am I wrong?

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:35.000
You're half right.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.310
But "sacrifice" is a bit off the mark.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.310
Why?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:44.180
I dislike ironclad plans. 
There's nothing fun about them.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:47.350
Especially one-sided games like this.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.280
Well, the responsibility

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.240
for that lies with the 
oblivious adults involved.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:53.690
Where are your collaborators?

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.800
Collaborators?

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.590
So you misunderstand me after all.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:05:59.870
What's so funny?

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.110
Logos isn't an organization.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.900
It's just a style,

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.040
for taking over the system known as Japan.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.710
Do you have no respect for 
Japan's history and culture—

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.730
Let's not talk about things like that.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.780
It's a system that moves a group of 
weak people who choose to lean

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.630
against the symbol called "Japan."

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:18.980
Can't we agree that's how it is?

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.440
But you all chose to come together, so—

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:27.190
To me, Mythos is just one pawn in the game.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.530
Mythos?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.030
It's a code name.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.030
Mine is Bird.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:38.060
Oh, I'll give you a hint to make 
the game more interesting.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.090
A hint?

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:42.560
Try to get Orochi's "ro" before Mythos.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.750
Orochi's "ro"...

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:48.020
The unified information Mythos has obtained 
is only from Orochi's "o" and "chi,"

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.390
so only half of the whole.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.570
After all, when faced with an external threat,

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:58.500
a defense system is activated whereby 
the most important data

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.390
<b>External Threat Detected</b>

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:02.530
in the deepest parts of the system, 
the "ro," is automatically deleted.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.890
<b>Deletion Sequence Initiated</b>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.750
But the Ministry of Internal 
Affairs and Communications

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.070
keeps a backup in a different location.

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.880
Confirm this with the MIAC.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:10.900
Yes, sir!

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.660
If Mythos secures "ro" first,

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.760
Japan will fall completely into Logos's...

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.790
No, Mythos's hands.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:31.800
What's in this building?

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.210
Who knows?

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:36.110
Making a 500-meter radius a no-entry zone

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:39.200
and ordering us to guard the place is a big deal.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.640
Whatever their reasons,

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.360
we'll just follow our orders.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:50.800
The MIAC has confirmed the backup's existence,

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.570
but they insist security is airtight.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:56.540
Is this the time for a turf war?!

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.910
They should at least share information 
with the government!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:03.610
For better or worse, this is what 
the nation has become.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.310
You can't expect them to change this 
"Japan style" at the drop of a hat.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.880
What should we do? Kichijouji isn't a small area.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.180
Let's divide the past cases among us, 
and see if we can dig up a lead.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.870
What exactly do we do, though?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.540
Look for a ghost, maybe?

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.230
S-Sorry!

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.190
Sorry! Sorry! I'm sorry!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.150
Sorry! Sorry! Sorry!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.150
You know you can't go out after 8 PM!

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.750
I'm sorry!

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.420
Go home!

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:38.370
Okay!

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.100
What's with all this ghost talk during a crisis?

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.610
This is the eighth report.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.010
Did you hear that?

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:45.460
Huh?

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:48.880
Look.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:56.100
It's not a ghost, is it?

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.340
Don't be stupid.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.690
Where'd the girl go?

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:06.490
Huh?

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.080
H-Hey, you can't be outside after 8 PM...

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.820
So, did you find anything, Kyoukai-kun?

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.870
Yes, it's just what I'd suspected.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:30.950
It's a hologram projector equipped 
with a motion detector.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:32.250
A motion detector?

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:36.840
The hologram has several patterns 
based on detected motion.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:40.900
Other traffic signals are probably rigged 
with the same kind of detector.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.880
So it was just some prank?

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:46.030
But is it just a prank?

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.380
The sightings are clustered around 
Musashisakai, Mitaka, Ogikubo,

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.730
Kamishakujii, and Kichijouji.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.790
Uh, is it okay for us

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:56.080
to be acting outside our jurisdiction?

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:00.450
The governor's been hospitalized, so we'll 
only face reprimand when he's discharged.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.450
Until then, let's do as we please.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:06.420
Um, this device is operated remotely.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:07.640
Remotely?

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:08.920
Under the current conditions?

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.810
It seems to use analog radio waves.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.100
First Dog, then Bird.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.630
Now we just need Monkey.

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.900
Soon, I think...

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.890
Mythos, win this fight if you want to be my equal.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:34.160
Sis?

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.440
Excuse us.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.320
Huh?

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.730
Oh, so this is the boss's hideout?

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.010
Stop! That's rude.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:41.410
He's right, Kuroki-san!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:42.520
Fine, fine.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:43.830
Wh-What's this about?

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.870
I'll explain later.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.500
Hinata, please stay here.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.090
You'll explain later?

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.210
Please.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:53.460
Okay.

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:55.140
Found it.

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:55.670
Huh?

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.430
It was being controlled from this laptop.

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:00.160
Controlled?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.180
Hinata, your laptop was being used

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:04.890
by Hachijou Tomoki.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:14.520
He snuck a program onto her laptop 
that booted the computer,

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.710
and then sent signals to a transmitter

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.590
that turned the motion sensor on and off.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:27.040
The more important issue is the file cleverly 
hidden in the transmission software.

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:28.790
A hidden file?

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:32.940
When you decrypt the file, 
there's another encrypted file inside.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.260
The last gate requires

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.920
<b>Voice Recognition Lock</b>

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.920
voice activation.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.150
I see.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:43.050
So it requires a spoken 
password to open the file.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.140
That's right.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:45.720
Open, tulip.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.510
<b>Vocal Input Incorrect</b>

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:47.510
See?

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:48.860
A password, huh?

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:51.630
We'll just have to make him cough it up,

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:54.220
but I doubt he'll be forthcoming.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:11:57.520
But this is his own game.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.860
There's no point in him making us do all this.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:02.230
Then there's a hint somewhere?

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:05.020
Hinata, do you have any thoughts on this?

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:09.630
Well, all I know is that he said something 
strange just as the police arrived...

00:12:10.050 --> 00:12:10.700
Oh!

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:11.320
What?

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:12.290
What happened?

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.250
When they came...

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:19.140
How about "I want your lip," then?

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.590
Heh, what a cool customer.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:24.680
That's what I thought, too,

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:28.750
but maybe the president meant "RIP."

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.240
"Rest in peace"?

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:31.380
Wait.

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.770
The original phrase is in Latin, isn't it?

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.520
And she'd have to speak the phrase herself.

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:38.230
Me?

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:39.480
Just try.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.940
Requiescat in pace.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.030
The file's open.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.200
Well done!

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.830
Hachijou set your voice pattern and that 
password as the decryption key.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.080
W-Wait a minute.

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:55.040
Does that mean he knew about the work you do?

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.990
I believe so.

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:02.100
Then, to him,

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:04.580
I was also just...

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:08.460
It's some kind of structure.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.320
It'd be best if we could run an image search,

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:12.720
but in our current state...

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.990
Wait! I've seen this building before.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.430
If I remember correctly, 
it's the one near Inokashira Park.

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.190
Oh, the Intelligent Building.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.340
That's where Orochi's "ro" is?

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:26.650
But we'll need permission from various 
agencies in order to sortie.

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:29.600
Those are the rules, but...

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:30.980
There's no time for that.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:32.850
If Orochi's "ro" is stolen,

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:35.190
Japan will fall completely under their rule.

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.830
This is not the time to be fixated on details.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:39.670
That's the first time we've agreed.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.300
If anything happens, I'll take responsibility.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.260
Don't be a hero, partner.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.130
Don't talk like that. It nauseates me.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:49.840
What?

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.790
Okay, that's enough.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:52.850
Boss?

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.130
Everyone...

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.440
Kobayashi-san!

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:07.760
Hey, I rushed down from my store on my bike.

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:11.180
My hobby happens to be amateur radio.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.830
So what's Funasaka-san's message?

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.580
Oh, yes.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:18.430
He wants you to rendezvous with them 
because they've learned where "ro" is.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:19.440
Really?

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:21.420
They're going to sortie.

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.350
Thank you, Kobayashi-san.

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:24.800
I'll go there right away.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:26.960
You won't do any such thing.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:31.530
Kazari-kun, Unit 8's Willwears 
aren't your personal property.

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.430
But, Director, right now...

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.640
Answer me.

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:37.030
What side are you on?

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:39.360
The police's or Unit 8's?

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:45.180
As a police officer assigned to Unit 8, 
I cannot disobey a superior's orders.

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.100
You need to learn more about politics.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:51.030
If you wish to become an important official, 
you must follow the government will.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:53.070
But right now...

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:55.080
I have no desire to listen to your pleas!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:58.840
You should just obey my orders, as your superior!

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.540
Then I approve. Go, Kazari-kun.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.460
D-Director General...

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:07.780
I authorize Unit 8 to sortie.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:11.840
You are the only ones capable 
of acting in this emergency.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:12.650
Yes, sir.

00:15:12.650 --> 00:15:14.230
But, sir...

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:18.040
You should just obey my orders, as your superior.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:22.080
I hereby order Special Public Security Fifth Division,

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.800
Third Mobile Assault Unit 8,

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:25.480
to protect Japan.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:27.650
Understood!

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:39.290
Unit 8? They picked up our trail 
faster than I expected.

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:12.900
Confirming switch to analog radio.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:13.740
Okay.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.450
Got it.

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:15.530
All good.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.870
Yes, I can hear you.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.330
Okay, let's go.

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:27.880
I knew they'd get here before us!

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.970
Terrorists...

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.340
Neutralize the enemy.

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:43.270
What?

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:47.400
Chief, the attackers are USDF Willwear units!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.130
Huh?

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:50.860
Why is the SDF attacking us?

00:16:51.350 --> 00:16:53.200
And they're not pulling any punches.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.320
They're clearly out for blood.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.150
IFF again? It makes a good trap.

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:00.080
We don't stand a chance!

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.000
Don't worry, we can win.

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:04.050
Are you sure?

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:06.090
We only need to secure one position.

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:06.810
That's right.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:10.000
Orochi's "ro" is protected by a door that will open

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.880
through simultaneous access via 
computer and physical key.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.400
Mythos not only has to open the door,

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:18.430
but also must reset administrator access.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.970
That will take time.

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:21.350
Got it.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.060
Everyone, return to the command 
vehicle and prepare for raid!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:24.980
Roger!

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:28.560
I've decrypted the password.

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:30.440
Dear SDF,

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:33.030
please buy me a little more time.

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:40.870
Go ahead.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:45.660
We are the police.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:48.040
Please cease resistance.

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:51.730
If you don't, we'll have to hurt you just a little.

00:17:56.910 --> 00:18:00.090
It's no use! They've cut off external audio mikes!

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:02.430
We have no choice. 
Deactivate all sublimation modules!

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:11.610
These terrorists know what they're doing.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:20.280
There are fewer terrorists? Wait a minute!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.150
Orochi's "ro" is two floors down?

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.670
No way... Miho?

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.050
Listen! In the basement, the National Public—

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.610
External communications have been shut off!

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.610
I'm here! Where is everyone?

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.690
Good, I just finished making adjustments.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.420
Please take this.

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:03.550
Whirling Slam!

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.580
I don't have time to fight you right now.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:27.430
A little more... Just a little more...

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.030
Boss, we can't last any longer!

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:48.410
Found it!

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:50.620
I found the SDF's command vehicle in the back!

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:54.080
Severing their comm link might 
return their IFF to normal.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.370
Oscar II!

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:03.400
C-Crap!

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.600
Simulation pattern Sakigake, activate!

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:14.440
Well done! My compliments!

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:15.620
Huh?

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.530
In accordance with the Secret Service Act,

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.780
I will now exercise material force.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:28.210
Destructive electro-vibration shock wave!

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.860
Head, respond.

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:34.680
Head!

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.270
The link's been severed...

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:43.090
Souichirou? Why are you here?

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:44.800
That's my line.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.510
Stop attacking! Stop right now!

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:57.880
Seems they identify you as an enemy now, too.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:05.820
Oscar I!

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:09.000
What's that?

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:12.250
The sleep-inducer from the 
giant humanoid incident.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.120
Now we only have to stop Mythos, right?

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:20.750
Yeah.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:22.130
The door's open!

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:30.880
Did we get here in time?

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:32.270
Or are we...

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:41.960
The net!

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:43.860
The net's back on-line!

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:50.030
The system's been regained, I see. Good!

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:52.240
Are you happy,

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:55.080
Japan style, the system that exiled me?

00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:59.000
But now, everything is mine...

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:00.960
<b>Password Reset</b>

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:00.960
I've won.

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:04.780
Why is Liko-chan up there?

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:07.840
<i>Sorry, everyone watching this screen.</i>

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:14.230
<i>Congratulations.</i>

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:16.360
<i>All devices with Liko installed</i>

00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:18.710
<i>now belong to Mythos.</i>

00:23:49.990 --> 00:23:51.860
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:51.860 --> 00:24:04.870
File 12: For Whom Does Order Exist?

00:23:52.780 --> 00:24:04.870
The sound you hear is an intentional decision by the director.
